# React + Vite

- Use functional components with the `function` keyword.
- Keep components small: one main job per component.
- Use `useState` for local UI state; do not add Redux/Zustand unless asked.
- Use `useEffect` only for side effects (fetch, subscriptions); clean up when needed.
- Always consider loading, empty, and error UI when calling the API.
- Colocate simple styles with the feature (`App.css`) or shared `index.css`; do not introduce Tailwind or CSS-in-JS unless asked.
- Prefer composition: smaller components over one giant file when the UI grows.
- Lists need a stable `key` prop (prefer real ids over array index when available).
- Do not use Next.js APIs (`Image`, `Link`, App Router, Server Components) — this app is Vite.
